{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The compiler lowers `printf(\"%s\\n\", line)` to `puts(line)`, and GCC 11.5 compiles the dangling-pointer helper to a null return at both `-O0` and `-O3`; consequently `bad()` emits nothing. I’m creating a dependency-free Rust `cdylib` with the four exact C signatures, a writable static C string for `good()`, libc `puts` for identical stream behavior, and the compiled null behavior for `bad()`."}}
